WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.440
So this is Volume 12, and we're taking up in November the 2nd, 1917.

2
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:12.640
So we're talking about chastisements for Italy.

3
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:17.560
Continuing my state amid privations, pains and bitterness,

4
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.960
especially because of the many evils that one hears about

5
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.880
and the entrance of foreigners into Italy,

6
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.240
I was praying good Jesus to stop the enemies and I said,

7
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.880
"Perhaps this was the flood you were talking about,

8
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.960
and this is very, very important."

9
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.840
When Jesus said there was a flood coming,

10
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.800
he meant an invasion.

11
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.880
So you need to understand that like the prophets of the Bible,

12
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.200
that words are used in a symbolic sense.

13
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.840
It doesn't necessarily mean a tsunami.

14
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.160
My daughter, he said, "The flood I was talking about

15
00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:55.160
was precisely this, and the flood will continue to flow and flow.

16
00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:58.680
The foreigners will continue to invade Italy."

17
00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:02.680
Now watch this, why is this chastisement coming?

18
00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:06.360
She has very much deserved it.

19
00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:10.720
I had chosen Italy as a second Jerusalem.

20
00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:11.920
This is terribly important.

21
00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.960
God the Father had chosen Jerusalem in Israel,

22
00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.000
and God the Son chose a second Jerusalem in Rome.

23
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.200
What I mean by that is that the center of the church

24
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.160
would be there, and the leadership of the church,

25
00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.320
because in Jerusalem you had the temple,

26
00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.520
and you had all the leadership of the Jewish faith.

27
00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.520
So that's the way it is in Rome.

28
00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.880
She in turn has disregarded my laws.

29
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:40.680
Now if you think they've changed,

30
00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.200
I haven't visited Rome for a couple of years now,

31
00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:48.120
but when I did, there are 400 churches and cathedrals

32
00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:51.560
in Rome, most of them empty and unused.

33
00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:54.360
She has disregarded my laws, has denied to me

34
00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:57.400
the rights which were my Jew.

35
00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:00.680
Ah, I can say that she no longer behaved like man,

36
00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.200
but a beast, isn't that incredible?

37
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.680
That's the very low level of behavior.

38
00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:09.320
And under the heavy scourge of the war,

39
00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.880
I was not even recognized.

40
00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:14.520
Now the presumption that the Lord had

41
00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:18.680
was that in disaster we would turn to Him in prayer,

42
00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:22.000
but you need some level of faith inside of you for that.

43
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.560
So if even the First World War did not make them turn to God,

44
00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.520
then it means things are really bad.

45
00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:33.120
And she wanted to go on as my enemy.

46
00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.040
Justly has she deserved this defeat,

47
00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:39.040
that's a defeat in battle,

48
00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.880
and I will continue to humiliate her to the dust.

49
00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:46.200
Now why does he continue to humiliate us?

50
00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.400
I want to give you Isaiah chapter two,

51
00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:53.120
and it's verse seven, nine, 11.

52
00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:56.200
The pride of man must be brought low

53
00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.840
in order to try and help him to come back to God.

54
00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:05.880
Isaiah chapter two, verses seven, nine, and 11.

55
00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:09.520
And Louisa interrupting him said,

56
00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:10.920
"Jesus, what are you saying?

57
00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.560
Poor homeland of mine.

58
00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.560
How torn you will be.

59
00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:19.560
Jesus have pity and stop this current flow of the foreigner."

60
00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:24.040
And Jesus said, "My daughter, to my sorrow,

61
00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:27.160
I have to allow the foreigner to advance."

62
00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.240
Now if you know your Old Testament,

63
00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:33.240
you will know that whenever the people of God

64
00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:37.760
really broke God's covenant and behaved in a beastly manner,

65
00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:41.400
he allowed foreign people to come in and invade them

66
00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.160
and actually conquer them

67
00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.240
and sometimes take them out in slavery.

68
00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.840
It happened with the Assyrians

69
00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.960
and the northern kingdom of Israel,

70
00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:54.440
the Babylonians and the southern kingdom of Judah.

71
00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.440
They were allowed to be taken out of the country altogether.

72
00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:00.480
But the southern kingdom of Judah

73
00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:03.920
actually repented in its exile in Babylon,

74
00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.440
so they were allowed to go back.

75
00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:07.120
The northern ones didn't repent,

76
00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.760
so they shifted all over the world.

77
00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:11.200
And that's one of the reasons,

78
00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.880
probably the reason why Jesus said

79
00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:16.760
he had come to seek and to find the lost sheep

80
00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:17.920
of the house of Israel

81
00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:20.280
because they were now scattered all over the world.

82
00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:23.360
So the church had to go all over the world

83
00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.240
to find the children of God.

84
00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:32.280
So Jesus said, "I have to allow the foreigner to advance.

85
00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:35.640
"You, because you do not love souls as I do."

86
00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.740
In other words, I love them divinely.

87
00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:42.720
You would want Italy's victory.

88
00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:46.840
But if Italy wins, it will be a ruin for souls.

89
00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:48.640
Their pride, listen to this,

90
00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.640
now only God could reveal this about us.

91
00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:53.960
Their pride would reach such a point

92
00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:57.520
as to ruin the little bit of good that's left in the nation.

93
00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:00.400
They would have pointed themselves out

94
00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.880
to the rest of the world

95
00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:04.480
as the nation that could do without God.

96
00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:08.480
Isn't that very interesting?

97
00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:11.680
And so, because the Lord can't allow that disaster

98
00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.760
to happen to the rest of humanity,

99
00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:16.160
it's got to bring this nation down.

100
00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:17.240
Isn't that very interesting?

101
00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:20.000
You couldn't get that from anyone but the Lord.

102
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.800
Am I daughter?

103
00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.480
He said, "The scourges will continue.

104
00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:24.960
"Towns will be devastated.

105
00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:27.320
"I will strip them of everything.

106
00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:31.000
"The poor and the rich, it'll all be the same.

107
00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:34.160
"They didn't want to know my laws.

108
00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:39.360
"They had made of the earth a God for each one,

109
00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:42.400
"and I by stripping them will make them recognize

110
00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.520
"what the earth is.

111
00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:46.240
"I will purify the earth by fire."

112
00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:49.960
Now, that purification by fire, if it is literal,

113
00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:53.720
hasn't happened yet, except in a limited manner

114
00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:57.320
in Australia and in America.

115
00:05:57.320 --> 00:06:00.480
Okay, "For the stench it gives off

116
00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:02.560
"is such that I cannot bear it."

117
00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:05.080
Now, that description I've just had for you

118
00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:07.160
is a very good description of Europe today.

119
00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:13.400
And so, if the Lord, at this early stage in the 20th century,

120
00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:16.160
taught that Italy should be severely chastised

121
00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:19.280
in order to bring it back to God,

122
00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:23.200
well, then Europe is absolutely ripe for it, okay?

123
00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:27.920
So, before I go on, I want to give you Hebrews 12, 29.

124
00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:30.120
Our God is a consuming fire.

125
00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:35.040
The fire is chastisement, if that's what you need.

126
00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:38.840
The fire is love, if that's where you are

127
00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:40.600
in your relationship with God.

128
00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:47.200
Matthew 25, 41, those who finally reject the Lord

129
00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:50.160
are sent to the everlasting fire.

130
00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:54.880
And two Peter three, 10 to 12.

131
00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:01.880
So Jesus said, "I will purify the earth by fire

132
00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:05.680
"for the stench it gives off is such that I cannot bear it.

133
00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:09.200
"Many will remain buried in the fire,

134
00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:13.560
"and in this way I will make the earth come to its senses.

135
00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.080
"It is necessary.

136
00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:18.320
"The salvation of souls requires it."

137
00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:22.080
So, he's more interested in the eternal destiny of souls

138
00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.280
than the comfort of bodies.

139
00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:28.920
I had told you about these scourges a long time before,

140
00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:33.120
the time has come, but not yet completely.

141
00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:35.360
More evils will come.

142
00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:40.160
So, he's telling her that this purification by fire will come.

143
00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:44.720
Now, notice it's 1917, and our blessed mother had said in Fatima

144
00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:48.480
in 1917 that the earth would be purified by fire.

145
00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:52.440
And she said that the fire would come down from heaven.

146
00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:57.200
Now, the fire that consumed Sodom and Gomorrah

147
00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:02.200
and the other cities that were in cochoots with them,

148
00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:04.280
that was a fire from heaven.

149
00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:05.720
And they were literally burnt.

150
00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:09.320
And when you go to Sodom and Gomorrah have been found,

151
00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:13.080
and you can still pick up the lumps of sulfur in your hand,

152
00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:15.960
and you can still light them, it's pure sulfur.

153
00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:19.160
And there are no volcanoes in the area

154
00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:23.080
within an aeroplane distance of the place.

155
00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:25.960
There's no earthquakes.

156
00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:28.560
Anyway, earthquakes don't produce sulfur.

157
00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:31.240
And usually, volcanoes don't either,

158
00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:34.320
because they produce the lava, okay?

159
00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:35.920
And so this was fire from heaven.

160
00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:38.520
And the evidence is still there.

161
00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:41.640
And the very interesting thing, you can get this on YouTube,

162
00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:45.800
the very interesting thing is what we thought were hills

163
00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:49.060
in the past are actually buildings covered with ash.

164
00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:54.640
I will purify the earth by fire

165
00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:58.000
for the stench it gives off, I cannot bear, he said.

166
00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.800
And so he's interested in the salvation of souls.

167
00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.520
I told you about this before,

168
00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:05.600
but the time is not completely ready yet.

169
00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:07.640
I will make the earth come to its senses.

170
00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:09.760
I will make the earth come to its senses.

171
00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:12.240
Now, you can see that that has not happened yet.

172
00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:14.000
The earth has not come to its senses.

173
00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:14.840
Has it? - Yeah.

174
00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:19.760
- And Louisa said, "My Jesus placates yourself enough for now."

175
00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:21.680
And he said, "I don't know, you pray,

176
00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:23.720
and I'll render the enemy less cruel."

177
00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.440
Okay, in other words, it has to happen.

178
00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:30.520
Now, November the 20th, 1917,

179
00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:32.880
you get the reason for the chastisement given.

180
00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:38.520
And also, he talks about the sanctity

181
00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:40.520
of living in the divine world.

182
00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:44.000
Continuing in my usual state, evermore painful,

183
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:48.160
my beloved Jesus comes and runs away like a flash.

184
00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:50.800
And he does not give me time even to pray him

185
00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:53.800
for the great evils that poor humanity is going through.

186
00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:56.960
Especially our dear homeland.

187
00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:58.200
What a blow to my heart,

188
00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.200
the entrance of foreigners into Italy.

189
00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.760
I thought that Jesus had told me this before

190
00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:05.760
in order to make me pray.

191
00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:08.320
And when he comes, if I pray him,

192
00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:10.520
he says to me, "I will be inexorable."

193
00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:12.560
In other words, it's gonna happen.

194
00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:15.920
But if I press him by saying to him,

195
00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:18.080
"Jesus, don't you want to have compassion?

196
00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:19.960
"Don't you see how towns are destroyed?

197
00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:23.120
"How people remain naked and starving?

198
00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:24.760
"Jesus, how hard you have become."

199
00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:26.560
He answers.

200
00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:29.520
I wanted to give a heading for the next paragraph.

201
00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:34.520
His concern is immortal souls, not material things.

202
00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:42.200
His concern is immortal souls, not material things.

203
00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:47.760
And if you've ever gone on a holiday to Italy,

204
00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:51.880
they have made the churches, museum pieces and art galleries.

205
00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:56.800
I remember hearing an hour's talk

206
00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:01.800
on the art in one tiny section of Maria Maggiore in Rome.

207
00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:05.640
They've turned them into art museums

208
00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:07.720
and people can get their art degrees

209
00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:10.240
by getting their lectures off these walls.

210
00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:12.760
But there's nobody praying in the place.

211
00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:15.040
Now, he's not interested in that.

212
00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:16.480
So Jesus said, "My daughter,

213
00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:20.560
"my daughter, I'm not concerned about the cities.

214
00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:24.440
"I'm not concerned about the great things of the earth.

215
00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:26.880
"I am concerned about souls."

216
00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:30.040
Cities and churches and the like,

217
00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:33.480
after they've been destroyed, can be re-done or rebuilt.

218
00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:36.680
Did I not destroy everything in the flood

219
00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:38.440
that's Genesis chapter seven?

220
00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:42.600
And then was it not rebuilt again?

221
00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:46.120
But if souls are lost, it's forever.

222
00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:52.000
There's no one who can give them back to me

223
00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:54.440
to see the issue there.

224
00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:57.960
"Ah, I cry for souls," he said.

225
00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:00.320
"They have denied heaven for the earth."

226
00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:04.120
Now, you're talking about atheistic materialism here.

227
00:12:04.120 --> 00:12:05.480
The buildings are important,

228
00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:07.040
the economy is important,

229
00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:10.080
everything is important except the soul.

230
00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.120
They have denied heaven for the earth

231
00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:14.040
and I will destroy the earth

232
00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:17.440
and I will make the most beautiful things disappear

233
00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:20.760
because these are like a rope binding him.

234
00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:23.480
Now, if that was so in 1917,

235
00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:27.000
it's infinitely much more worse now.

236
00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:30.240
Okay, so people are literally bound to the earth

237
00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:32.080
and he's not going to allow it to happen.

238
00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:34.640
So I want to give you a few references there.

239
00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:36.440
Hebrews 11, 10.

240
00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:40.740
Hebrews 11, 10.

241
00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:45.280
And also verses 13 to 16.

242
00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:52.840
And I want to give you Sam, 49.

243
00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:56.560
Sam, 49 is a wonderful Sam

244
00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:58.600
and if you want a summary of it,

245
00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:00.600
you'll get it in Shakespeare.

246
00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:03.480
Shakespeare said they strut and fret their hour

247
00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:06.480
upon the stage and then they are heard no more.

248
00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:10.840
Now, Sam, 49 is where Shakespeare got it.

249
00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:14.840
He talks about people having huge estates of their own

250
00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:16.320
and servants running after them

251
00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:18.480
and then they're all heard it into shale

252
00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:20.840
and they never heard of again.

253
00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:22.480
That's where Shakespeare got it.

254
00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:25.840
It's the only reference I know where Shakespeare got it.

255
00:13:25.840 --> 00:13:29.040
That's Sam, 49, it's a wonderful Sam.

256
00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:35.640
And so, Louisa said, Jesus, what are you saying?

257
00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:38.600
And he said, courage, do not lose heart.

258
